  "faq-item-a-0": "One plan: 190 Kč a month excl. VAT (instead of 990 Kč) when you take card payments through us, plus 0,9 % + 1 Kč per card payment. That is our fee, always the same whatever your revenue; the third-party fees on top are <a class=\"mif-link\" href=\"#mif\">itemised below</a>. First 14 days are free, and if you’re not happy we give you your money back. No tiers, no catch, no contract.",
  "faq-item-a-1": "MIF++ is how a card fee is itemised, so you can see who gets what. We add nothing on top of it: the same fees are in there as in a single “blended” rate, they just aren’t hidden in one number. Every card payment carries:\n          <ul class=\"a-list\">\n            <li><b>0,9 % + 1 Kč to us</b> for processing the payment, always the same, whatever your revenue.</li>\n            <li><b>The interchange fee (MIF)</b> to the bank that issued your guest’s card.</li>\n            <li><b>The scheme fee</b> to Visa or Mastercard.</li>\n          </ul>\n          We neither set nor keep the last two, they go on in full. For consumer cards issued in the EEA the interchange fee is capped by EU law at 0,2 % (debit) and 0,3 % (credit). Rates differ by card type, and meal-voucher, AMEX and Diners cards carry an extra fee. All prices and fees exclude VAT. You have enough paperwork without us, so we tried to write this so it reads once. The cap on the interchange fee was filled in on your behalf in Brussels: the one form you never have to see.",
